`build/button.ino.bin` and `build/button.ino.partitions.bin` are built from
`firmware/button/button.ino` with Arduino CLI 1.5.1 and esp32:esp32 3.3.12, fqbn
`esp32:esp32:esp32s3`. That is the ESP32S3 Dev Module defaults: USB CDC on boot disabled, PSRAM
disabled, 4MB flash, the default partition table, QIO 80MHz, and the sketch on core 1. The
sketch is copied into an empty temporary directory and compiled from there, with
`SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH=1767225600` and
`-ffile-prefix-map=$work=/src -ffile-prefix-map=$build=/build -ffile-prefix-map=$HOME/.arduino15=/arduino15`
on the C, C++ and assembler flags. `$work` is that directory, `$sketch` is `$work/button`,
`$build` is the build directory and `$out` is the output directory. The command, run with `$work`
as the working directory, is `SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH=1767225600 arduino-cli compile --clean --fqbn esp32:esp32:esp32s3 --jobs 2 --build-path "$build" --output-dir "$out" --build-property "compiler.c.extra_flags=$map" --build-property "compiler.cpp.extra_flags=$map" --build-property "compiler.S.extra_flags=$map" "$sketch"`.
Two such builds in different directories are the same bytes. The app is 301696 bytes,
8fff3bc353ce8a857959f81216a382887adbd50b0aad382039cd855b1d22bf5b. The ELF is
df3d5cb3419eb722a2ed69a58e7c7d064e6d9e5151f789270bfcbb2e3a78392d. The partition table is 3072
bytes, 148b959cbff1c38aa8e1d5c0ba9d612c54997b945e56a63f41223eef650653a1. The chip starts where
the bootloader leaves the app, so the image needs neither the bootloader nor the merged binary.

